                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Over two years and somebody has finally delivered a working VR fun round of golf. Don't get me wrong the more professional approach taken by the Golf Club has great working mechanics, but im sure im not the only one that finds it a little less fun when the realisation kicks in that your no type of golfer.\n\nThis is the Hotshots approach. The character creation is extensive, the 8 courses will take you an age to get through, looking at the screens of the other courses there appears to be variety.\n\nOn the course taking the shot was simple enough, you won't need to try too hard to to get full distance on a driver or iron shots. Non the less though, it retains the satisfaction of playing a shot. The chip shots need some work, they seem a little floaty and playing from a bunker seems no different than playing from a fairway, A more visual representation of wind would be good, and perhaps some kind of visual behind the golfer to indicate the arc of a full swing. I have a few more suggestions that could improve things to make it a little more appealing to the Hotshot product it wants to be.\n\nAll said though, this is very much that golf game i've wanted since i first played Cloudlands. The simple fun you had when you first picked up the putter in cloudlands has been replicated here.\n\nFor the cost you won't be short changed if your here just for a single player game, if multiplayer works then it's an absolute bargain for the price.",
